---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
const services = [
  ['01','Trip design','Turn the group, shared interest, timing, or destination idea into a coherent travel concept.'],
  ['02','Travel coordination','Flights, lodging, local transport, activities, operators, and the dependencies between them.'],
  ['03','Organizer support','Give the trip leader a clear process, useful answers, and less administrative weight to carry alone.'],
  ['04','Traveler readiness','Clarify documents, equipment, fitness, expectations, timing, and what participants need before departure.'],
  ['05','Group communications','Create a more orderly path from initial interest through decisions, preparation, and final trip information.'],
  ['06','Launch support','Help organizers present the trip clearly to their own club, community, team, or audience when needed.']
];
const groupTypes=['Outdoor & hiking clubs','Dive & watersports communities','Wellness & studio groups','Social & affinity communities','Business & team groups','Organizer-hosted departures'];
---
<BaseLayout title="Private Group Travel | Talon Expeditions" description="Custom, fully supported private group travel for clubs, communities, businesses, studios, affinity groups and organizers." image={images.group}>
  <section class="page-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.group}')`}><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Private Group Travel</p><h1 class="section-title">Build the trip around your people, not a generic departure.</h1><p>For clubs, communities, businesses, studios, affinity groups, friends, and organizers who want the experience tailored and the difficult parts coordinated.</p></div></section>

  <section class="specialty-intro"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">What Talon handles</p><h2 class="section-title">A travel partner for the organizer and the travelers.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">The offer is split into the actual work required to move a group from idea to departure, rather than treating private travel as one generic service.</p></div><div class="donor-grid">{services.map(([n,t,c])=><div class="donor-card"><span class="card-index">{n}</span><h3>{t}</h3><p>{c}</p></div>)}</div></div></section>

  <section class="section tabbed-feature"><div class="shell tabbed-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Who we build for</p><h2 class="section-title">Different groups need different trips.</h2><ul class="category-menu">{groupTypes.map((item,i)=><li class={i===0?'active':''}>{item}</li>)}</ul></div><div class="category-feature" style={`background-image:url('${images.wildlife}')`}><div class="feature-note"><h3>Group-first does not mean one-size-fits-all.</h3><p>A hiking club, dive community, company team, and wellness studio may all travel as groups, but their pace, risk, communication, and support needs are completely different.</p></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell process-donor"><div class="process-visual" style={`background-image:url('${images.planning}')`}><div class="process-callout"><h3>You bring the people.</h3><p>We can start before the destination, itinerary, or final group size is fixed.</p></div></div><div><p class="eyebrow">The planning path</p><h2 class="section-title">From an organizer’s idea to a trip people can understand and prepare for.</h2><p class="section-copy">Avero’s process section is adapted here to the actual Talon operating model.</p><div class="process-list"><div class="process-item"><b>Define the Trip</b><p>Group, purpose, activity, timing, comfort, approximate budget, and constraints.</p></div><div class="process-item"><b>Shape the Plan</b><p>Destination, itinerary, suppliers, lodging, transport, support level, and terms.</p></div><div class="process-item"><b>Prepare to Launch</b><p>Present the trip clearly, answer participant questions, and organize commitments.</p></div><div class="process-item"><b>Prepare to Travel</b><p>Documents, readiness, final information, coordination, and departure support.</p></div></div><a class="button" href="/contact/">Start a Group Planning Conversation</a></div></div></section>

  <section class="quote-strip"><div class="shell"><strong>The organizer should not have to become a full-time travel coordinator.</strong><p>Talon’s role is to make the moving parts coherent enough that the leader can concentrate on the community they are bringing together.</p></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Questions organizers usually have</p><h2 class="section-title">Start before everything is decided.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">Private group travel works best when planning starts with the real constraints instead of hiding them until the end.</p></div><div class="faq-list"><details open><summary>Do we need a final group size before we talk?</summary><p>No. An approximate range is enough to start shaping the trip and understanding what changes as the group grows or shrinks.</p></details><details><summary>Can Talon work with a trip our organization already has in mind?</summary><p>Yes. We can start with a destination, a route, an event, an activity, or a partially formed itinerary and determine where support is useful.</p></details><details><summary>Can the trip be built for mixed ability levels?</summary><p>Often yes. The design needs to account for pace, optional activities, support, and honest readiness requirements rather than pretending every traveler has the same needs.</p></details><details><summary>Can you help us communicate or launch the trip?</summary><p>Organizer-facing support can include structuring the offer and helping make the trip easier for your members, clients, staff, or community to understand.</p></details></div></div></section>

  <section class="specialty-cta"><div class="shell"><h2>Have the group but not the whole plan?</h2><a class="button button-secondary" href="/contact/">Build It With Talon</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
